nd fairness: resource allocation under the Ryan White CARE Act</article-title><source>Health Affairs</source><year>2006</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>1103</fpage><lpage>1112</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16835192</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1377/hlthaff.25.4.1103</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jabine</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name><name><surname>Louis</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schirm</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><collab>Eds</collab></person-group><source>Choosing the Right Formula: Initial Report Panel on Formula Allocations Committee on National Statistics, Division of Behavioral and Social Sciences and Education, National Research Council of the National Academies</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Washington DC: National Academies Press</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nap.edu/catalog.php?record_id=10178"/><comment>Accessed June 7, 2006</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Louis</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Jabine</surname><given-names>TB</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerstein</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><collab>Eds</collab></person-group><source>Statistical Issues in Allocating Funds by Formula Panel on Formula Allocations, Committee on National Statistics, Division of Behavioral and Social Sciences and Education, National Research Council of the National Academies</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Washington DC: National Academies Press</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.nap.edu/catalog/10580.html#toc"/><comment>Accessed June 7, 2006</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cantrell<